"There are two ways to make yourself harder to tip. First, spread your feet. A bigger base gives that line more room to move before it reaches the edge. Second, bend your knees. A lower center of gravity has to swing farther before the line reaches the edge. Athletes do both. Watch a judo player or a basketball defender: feet wide, knees bent. But a base is only wide in the direction you spread your feet. Feet side by side resist a push from the side. One foot in front resists a push from the front.": "7b4604d7e6a0",
